  {
   "key": "0x04..0x07",
   "name": "control port",
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
     "lines": "914-918"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
     "function": "sega315_5313_device::ctrl_port_w"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
     "function": "sega315_5313_device::update_code_and_address"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "MAME's vdp_w answers byte offsets 0x04 and 0x06 alike with ctrl_port_w, logging a write that does not touch both byte lanes.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "897",
       "sha": "e6943f4dd1aca982e94b629815b8ee80db7416b96b72dc8532e82f6689b9ae30"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "914-917",
       "sha": "0960df00862075551a91ca1e51c62da61875d87decc22d17781b227d7db9fb88"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "102",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "A control port write cancels a pending fill.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "858",
       "sha": "a28dca754df44868e5e3b31fbb8e686c8f223367dd5fa47e6a2514e8656af9a3"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "103",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "With a first word pending, the word is stored as the second one, the pending flag clears, and code and address are recomputed.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "860-866",
       "sha": "1b23ce8d2b38869e0ff3c4aef0515c856b61a1cff38bada8063c51ea71430e3c"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "104",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "With none pending, a word whose bits 15 and 14 are 10 sets the register numbered by bits 13 to 8 to its low byte and clears code and address.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "860",
       "sha": "5faac3f4a04e392520038e1aa495134185af6e2211154ca5a81442edc0ff3282"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "872-873",
       "sha": "45d645723aed811fd272a52f23b70458dc70ab35b01c090c0193c8c762c5385e"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "874-884",
       "sha": "baefdd7516e9008850f3f08e92f73b89cd4dae15b1ee56515edcf2cd4a1b6183"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "105",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "Bit 5 of that register number, bit 13 of the control word, is logged as a register error and the number is masked to five bits.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "876",
       "sha": "87d155546e02cdf852269913c6a0e71c4d3c5eea4910adad8a706833ca791f5f"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "879",
       "sha": "85cc98594902c919849766c687cfc4ebeef30f3f71b94ee24561a6a43982302a"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "881",
       "sha": "cfe7a948a205b68fd221fc4d3454298019375cef398b814cd5021d3f48269b85"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "106",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "Any other word with none pending is stored as the first word, sets the pending flag and sets code and address from it.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "860",
       "sha": "5faac3f4a04e392520038e1aa495134185af6e2211154ca5a81442edc0ff3282"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "872-873",
       "sha": "45d645723aed811fd272a52f23b70458dc70ab35b01c090c0193c8c762c5385e"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "885-889",
       "sha": "1470d5abe958d76a703df8a5809974720239552993f6b412f95dc8ac31e517e0"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "107",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "The code is bits 15 and 14 of the first word plus bits 7 to 4 of the second shifted right by 2.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "633-634",
       "sha": "fc80df64ba2c2cfb9c0b17dc0ed5789640ab0e8d724bbefe1186ed7e052c0ab8"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "108",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "The address is bits 13 to 0 of the first word plus bits 1 and 0 of the second shifted left by 14.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "636-637",
       "sha": "db1715eacf109e85a29f1db4b9d434aeaac92fb8b2f3960c86c56a95580dd944"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "109",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "After the second word, a code with bit 5 set starts DMA handling by calling handle_dma_bits.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "860",
       "sha": "5faac3f4a04e392520038e1aa495134185af6e2211154ca5a81442edc0ff3282"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "863-868",
       "sha": "27f5e7ee7fff27eb6e12d5ef974475b74a1870bcbd3b686d0e22b52800a3ad84"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.h",
       "lines": "137",
       "sha": "e926c6d3b84e98fc41b98bcbe9cdffacb0f336a2cfcfd138b7c204a4b8acddc0"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "access": "write",
   "closed": [
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
     "lines": "918",
     "as": "structure"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "key": "0x08..0x0F",
   "name": "HV counter",
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
     "lines": "1338-1346"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
     "function": "sega315_5313_device::megadriv_read_hv_counters"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
     "function": "sega315_5313_device::get_hposition"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
     "function": "sega315_5313_device::get_scanline_counter"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
     "function": "sega315_5313_device::screen_hpos"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
     "function": "sega315_5313_device::get_hres"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "MAME's vdp_r answers byte offsets 0x08, 0x0A, 0x0C and 0x0E alike with megadriv_read_hv_counters.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "1318",
       "sha": "e6943f4dd1aca982e94b629815b8ee80db7416b96b72dc8532e82f6689b9ae30"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "1338-1343",
       "sha": "6d7b8295ddd3afacf011b8a69c54de9d696a19f271babab9ed4c43fc2770dc2b"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "102",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "The word has the V counter in its high byte and the H counter in its low byte.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "1311",
       "sha": "130b3858f5a06075a1412bd590269db98407b572469cebf415c4026ca36507ea"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "103",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "The V counter is the scanline counter, plus 1 above horizontal position 460, looked up in a table by line count (register 0x01 bit 3) and NTSC or PAL.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "1285",
       "sha": "8f44ccbec5ab678c2048a2c845246aa4fbe70122a547043edd3614232c90097c"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "1289",
       "sha": "4fb1f437cdda3cb3257906402d11c075ce973d62f1f8fa662f327fad06539df2"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "1298-1307",
       "sha": "2eb6d7e188b33d4c47b9865708005201d65efa1b9932679033e3125f150d4bf9"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "81",
       "sha": "4c527a16ca5ecbecc17374abe0603fc56e9210235e367f9f95ab0a968437dc79"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "104",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "The H counter is the horizontal position, less 0x49 when it is above 0xF7.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "1309",
       "sha": "dd8c445e34ab04e94ec7462ad6f87bbce386c40ede0b69cc0f7a8e5bd8f5de60"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "105",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "The horizontal position is the elapsed fraction of the scanline time times 480, clamped to 480; with alternate timing or no frame rate it is the screen position.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "172",
       "sha": "5403ffd750e1867b5c0ee57e8058b53ecb8ce438a554c5cb85d4e694bee96c36"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "1247-1258",
       "sha": "64421d447de57ef95ac72f3d2abc0330877f1df96212712d94db5d9a09f41a1b"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "1259-1267",
       "sha": "5bffea35cdba73dbcc32a1a9312e05057e7eb623042a9efebdfcefbd6b4904ef"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "111",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "The scanline counter is m_scanline_counter, or the screen's vertical position when alternate timing is in use.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/315_5313.cpp",
       "lines": "1272-1275",
       "sha": "742e2db1fc6a6bb101724a87dd4fdc436fab7749ab93cc8a285249b7bfe3bc27"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "112",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "With alternate timing the screen's horizontal position is divided by 5 or 4, by register 0x0C bit 0, when m_lcm_scaling is set.",
     "quotes": [
      {
